{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of Petersen's theorem: a finite 3-regular graph in which no edge is a bridge has a perfect matching; moreover, every edge of such a graph lies in some perfect matching. Both statements are derived from Tutte's theorem (in Mathlib) by counting the edges that leave the odd components.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Juan Pablo Traverso Gianini"
    }
  ],
